          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TenantPoolLimitView"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "common.json#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Set Tenant Pool Limit",
        "tags": [
          "cloud_pool"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "description": "The cloud pool. On the operator plane, under /v1/admin/*, an operator who\nmay write sets the pool's limits, a new version each time: the VMs kept\nwarm, running and hibernated, the most VMs it holds at once, and the most one tenant holds; and a\ntenant's own maximum, or clears it. Each claim reads them as they stand,\nso a write holds with no deploy. A limit is written whole, so the write is\na PUT and a retry lands the same values, with no Idempotency-Key. Each\nwrite leaves an entry that names the operator: the pool's own in the\nplatform's stream, which no tenant reads, and a tenant's own in the\ntenant's.",
      "name": "cloud_pool"
    }
  ]
}
